# Detangler

Product spec: [`docs/GENESIS.md`](../../docs/GENESIS.md) (draft comb).
Family and app variant: [`docs/FAMILY.md`](../../docs/FAMILY.md).
Architecture: [`docs/PHASE_1_BRIEF.md`](../../docs/PHASE_1_BRIEF.md).
Do not fold the app comb into the draft skill.

Use **Detangler** for the family and the draft comb. Say "drafts"
or "the app comb" when the variant is not obvious. Header lockup:
*A structural pass for drafts that have been worked over.* Hero may
still use *Combs the whole document, not single strands.* — that
line is opaque in the header by itself.

The job is drafts that have been **worked over** — by one person, by
several, and especially by an agent. A lot of editing tangles
references, argument, repetition, and weight. Cutting or reordering
is one cause, not the product.

The **skill** is the product. An agent reads it and writes
`report.md`. npm ships the folders. There is no command-line comb.
Do not emit line-level suggestions in `report.md`.

Site and README speak as the product (Detangler / it). No corporate we.
No builder I. Same register as aiBreze: direct, no helper theater.
